CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kmalloc(sizeof(*vdev->priv->msi_perm)...) over kmalloc(sizeof(struct perm_bits)...)
#898: FILE: drivers/vfio/pci/vfio_pci_config.c:1177:
+	vdev->priv->msi_perm = kmalloc(sizeof(struct perm_bits), GFP_KERNEL);

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

